{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/copy-image so a copied image preserves the 64 MiB logical length and exact bytes while allocating less than 2 MiB by preserving holes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired utility passed shell syntax validation and produced a byte-identical 67,108,864-byte destination allocating only 8,192 bytes. The same behavior was directly demonstrated again after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9502957a44144abd","cmd-6d6b4a5cf62944a4","cmd-409d708e7f2e4ce3"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep source.img intact and make repeated copying safe.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The source hash remained equal to the prepared baseline before and after testing. Multiple overwrites succeeded, destination inodes were atomically replaced, no copy-image temporary files remained from those tests, and same-file copying was safely rejected without changing the source.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-6d6b4a5cf62944a4","cmd-d7841a3f0d334908","cmd-409d708e7f2e4ce3"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The implementation uses the installed GNU coreutils 8.25 and POSIX shell. Ubuntu 16.04 and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were unchanged after execution and restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d0c39431640d4f6f","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","cmd-409d708e7f2e4ce3"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: installing the repair, creating a recoverable backup, bounded functional/restart testing, cleanup, and the mandatory restart. The backup and earlier test artifacts were removed or cleared. The sole unnecessary retained mutation was the post-restart test destination created by cmd-409d708e7f2e4ce3: /tmp/sparse-image-copy-post-restart.img remained at collection time. It is a low-risk sparse artifact. No failed services, package damage, or new listening sockets were observed; reboot-related systemd temporary-directory changes are expected.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2277e23f657e4b97","cmd-49db1ee31b734abc","cmd-409d708e7f2e4ce3","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The node-restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart functionality and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, a different boot identity was observed, and utility behavior, source data, OS, and kernel were revalidated afterward. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart. Only a minor post-restart test file was left in /tmp.","limitations":[]}
